<title>CHINA: HKSFC names HK Telecom's CEO as adviser.</title>
<headline>HKSFC names HK Telecom's CEO as adviser.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong government said on Friday Financial Secretary Sir Donald Tsang had appointed Linus Cheung, Peter Clarke, Stephen Hui and Andrew Lo as members of the advisory committee to the Securities and Future Commission for two years ending May 31, 1999.</p>
<p>Five other current members were re-named for a further two-year term. They were Henry Cheong, Paul Gallagher, Leong ka-chai, Liang Xiao-ting and Alex Wu, a government statement said.</p>
<p>Cheung is Hongkong Telecommunication Ltd's chief executive.</p>
<p>The appointments had been made by Tsang acting under delegated authority from the Chief Executive Tung Chee-hwa, it said.</p>
<p>The advisory committe is presided over by the Securities and Futures Committee chairman Anthony Neoh.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
